                <pb facs="0343" n="229" sameAs="frus:frus1931v01/pg229"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">462.00R296/4713: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Portugal</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Magruder</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Lisbon</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-07-25T22:00:00+01:00">July 25, 1931—10
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received July 25—9:05 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>28. My telegram No. 27, July 24, 8 p.m.<anchor n="27" xml:id="d190-f1"/>
                    Following communication published this morning: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“On the 18th instant official notification was given of acceptance in
                            principle by the Portuguese Government of the Hoover proposal with
                            certain reservations relating primarily to the reparations in kind which
                            have special importance for Portugal. There has been sent to London a
                            Portuguese expert who is handling the matter there.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Magruder</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
